invariant: INV-69
file: src/keccak_neon.c
catches: keccak_neon_equiv_test
reason: the plain form's theta rotates each column parity by 2 and not by 1,
  so d[x] is wrong in every round. The plain form runs under every
  compiler, and the equivalence test runs it on every arm64 host.

--- old
    return veorq_u64(x, vsriq_n_u64(vshlq_n_u64(y, 1), y, 63));
--- new
    return veorq_u64(x, vsriq_n_u64(vshlq_n_u64(y, 2), y, 62));
